WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.310
In 1970, two scientists fused a mouse cell
and a human cell into one single cell.

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.930
At 37 degrees Celsius,
within about 40 minutes,

3
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.230
something on its surface
had completely changed.

4
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.200
Cool the cell to 15 degrees Celsius,
and that change almost stopped.

5
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.900
So how can you show that the molecules
in a membrane never stop moving?

6
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.170
In this mission, you'll find
out what those scientists did,

7
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.500
and read the data for warm and cold cells.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.300
Then you'll judge which observations really
count as evidence that membrane molecules

9
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.480
move.

10
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: find out how to show that
a membrane's molecules never stop moving.
